() Tj T*
(| Source | Requirement and implementation |) Tj T*
(| --- | --- |) Tj T*
(| TP3 pp.1-3; 08.4 slide 11 | Dynamic RPN with stable symbol references, types, uses, lexical scopes and ) Tj T*
(declaration-order lookup. Existing scope guards also restore discarded definitions. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.5 | Independent executable function and method bodies, ordered formal parameter metadata, copy ) Tj T*
(semantics, primitive RET and default zero of the declared primitive type. |) Tj T*
(| TP2 p.4; TP3 p.7 | Mandatory evaluation order, matching counts and argument-to-formal association. ) Tj T*
(Argument fragments are copied in the requested order using separate pending frames. |) Tj T*
(| TP2 p.7; TP3 pp.10-11 | Positional member access, existence, visibility and inherited lookup. Effective) Tj T*
( attributes are used consistently for access, copies and structural comparison. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.9 | Class codes are retained; equal-code classes are checked when complete. Copies between ) Tj T*
(distinct classes require matching codes. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.8; 08.3 slides 31-33 | Compile-time values and semantic attributes. A post-parse pass evaluates ) Tj T*
(known state and replaces compile-time reads with constants. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.6 | FROM retains strict comparisons and updates the control variable's current value after the ) Tj T*
(body. Compile-time-dependent loops process those updates on each expanded iteration. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.4; 08.3 slide 66 | General runtime numeric compatibility remains in the later RPN-to-assembler ) Tj T*
(translation. Evaluating a compile-time binding requires a representable value of its declared type. |) Tj T*
(| 08.3 slide 78 | Explicit TOI remains in RPN; the compile-time evaluator can evaluate it when its ) Tj T*
(operand is known. |) Tj T*
(| TP3 p.12 | Successful output contains numbered, readable RPN and TS metadata; diagnostics include ) Tj T*
(source lines. Debug traces are opt-in. |) Tj T*
