(## Class schemas) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Own declarations remain separate from effective attributes. Bases are traversed) Tj T*
(in source order, recursively placing their inherited attributes first; own) Tj T*
(attributes follow. This traversal order is an explicit representation convention.) Tj T*
(It never grants first-base priority when distinct inherited declarations conflict.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The same declaration reached through multiple paths is included once. Distinct) Tj T*
(homonymous inherited declarations remain subject to topic 32 ambiguity checks.) Tj T*
(Cycles produce diagnostics instead of leaving a traversal running indefinitely.) Tj T*
(Member lookup also works from within derived methods, following lexical lookup) Tj T*
(and the inherited member rules.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Classes with the same code must have the same number of effective attributes and) Tj T*
(the same declared type at each position. Attribute names and method signatures do) Tj T*
(not participate. Class-valued attribute types retain their qualified symbol) Tj T*
(identity. Copies are abstract value copies between corresponding effective) Tj T*
(positions; the backend must not copy by attribute name or alias object storage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Known integer positions are checked statically. Unknown positions remain symbol) Tj T*
(references with their receiver and class schema for TP4. A determinable position) Tj T*
(is required when it may select compile-time storage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Compile-time processing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Parsing retains expression fragments, complete function bodies and structured) Tj T*
