(control boundaries in dynamic RPN. Symbol references are resolved at their source) Tj T*
(occurrence, before this later pass, preserving declaration-order visibility.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(`specialize.c` processes these bodies with an environment per activation. It) Tj T*
(tracks known numeric values, runtime writes and pending argument copies. It does) Tj T*
(not mutate a global compile-time environment merely by parsing a function body.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Compile-time assignments update the environment and compile-time reads become) Tj T*
(constant references. Pure removed computations are discarded. If a removed) Tj T*
(assignment encloses runtime effects, those effects remain and DROP consumes the) Tj T*
(unused value. No runtime storage assignment for a compile-time symbol survives) Tj T*
(successful specialization. The final TS records main compile-time values and) Tj T*
(function-instance local compile-time bindings.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Known selections process their selected path for compile-time effects. Unknown) Tj T*
(selections retain branches and reject compile-time modifications at the responsible) Tj T*
(assignment, even if both branches would write the same value. Runtime knowledge) Tj T*
(is joined conservatively across branches. Syntax and name checks still cover the) Tj T*
(source as it is parsed, including paths later eliminated by specialization.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FROM loops with compile-time modifications are expanded while control is known.) Tj T*
(The body and its update are processed each iteration, so body changes to the) Tj T*
(control variable are respected. Other loops retain BF/BI. Calls invalidate the) Tj T*
(runtime values they may modify rather than treating unrelated state as changed.) Tj T*
(Unknown control cannot hide a compile-time modification inside a called function. Effect summaries ) Tj T*
(include indexed writes and whole-object copies involving compile-time attributes. Cached calls replay ) Tj T*
(only their actual effects instead of restoring unrelated captured state; known runtime writes are ) Tj T*
(propagated when the body proves their values.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Source functions requiring compile-time parameters or captured compile-time state) Tj T*
(are templates in the TS. Concrete instances receive `$ctN` labels linked to their) Tj T*
(source function. Bindings and activation state remain separate between instances.) Tj T*
(An uninvoked context-dependent template does not require a concrete executable) Tj T*
(instance; its body is retained during compilation. Ordinary declared functions) Tj T*
(are emitted even when uncalled. Recursive ordinary calls reuse an in-progress) Tj T*
(instance instead of being expanded during compilation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(POUT and ordinary stores remain runtime effects. No output operation is executed) Tj T*
(by the compiler. General runtime numeric type checking is not performed by this) Tj T*
(pass. Numeric values materialized for compile-time bindings use the language's) Tj T*
(INTEGER/SINGLEF representations, with explicit TOI when needed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Expansion has a 100,000-iteration budget and specialization a depth limit of 128.) Tj T*
(Exceeding these reports an evaluation resource limit and suppresses output. These) Tj T*
(are compiler resource limits, not language rules requiring BY to be positive or) Tj T*
(requiring ordinary runtime recursion to terminate at compile time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Calls and returns) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FRAME prepares a pending activation. Argument expressions are evaluated in the) Tj T*
(caller and ordinary ARG destinations receive copies in the specified order.) Tj T*
(Compile-time formals are bound in the specialization environment instead. CALL) Tj T*
(selects the prepared executable instance and leaves its result as an operand.) Tj T*
(Nested calls cannot overwrite a different pending activation's parameters.) Tj T*
(Object arguments also snapshot their compile-time attributes at the ARG copy,) Tj T*
(not after the remaining arguments have run. MATERIALIZE overlays the constants) Tj T*
(of that logical value onto its runtime fields; its OBJECT_VALUE TS record retains) Tj T*
(the original field declarations and constants. This preserves copies between) Tj T*
(compatible classes even when corresponding attributes have different compile-time) Tj T*
(qualifiers. Destination compile-time fields are bound in the compile-time) Tj T*
(environment and are not allocated or assigned by the runtime copy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Methods retain their receiver through FRAME/CALL. Unqualified method invocations) Tj T*
(inherit the active receiver. An inherited method's implicit attribute access and) Tj T*
(its receiver's positional access refer to the same declaration and object state.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Return headers must name INTEGER or SINGLEF. Object-valued return expressions) Tj T*
(are rejected. This restriction does not remove class-valued parameters, object) Tj T*
